+# Projects migration inventory v2
+
+Inventory **2.0.0** supersedes the frozen v1 inventory for the approved Story 6.6 supported read enrollment. It adds T01–T04 as `replace / include` while retaining all **11 MCP resources, five maintenance tools, 18 Frozen CLI spellings and 12 compatibility variants** below as `defer / exclude`. No legacy surface is retired.
+
+The successor baseline is `ce71717a965eb21454b3e13068b9072404dac5f5`. Historical source observations and A1 remain tied to v1's `3d256e632a7645bc2261e668ac7c74be81155f58` pin. The four new declarations and local candidate replace the historical conclusion that Projects has no enrollable Contracts. All tables remain migration/test artifacts outside `src/`, never runtime configuration. The companion [FrontComposer inventory](frontcomposer-migration-inventory-v1.md) retains its independent retirement gates.
+
+## Story 6.6 successor decision (2026-11-15)
+
+Jerome approved the four supported read queries under Projects `_bmad-output/planning-artifacts/sprint-change-proposal-2026-11-15-schedule-stories-6-8-and-6-6.md` §E8 on 2026-11-15, as restated in the Story 6.6 spec (D3, D5–D8 and Tasks & Acceptance). This is session approval only under A1’s limits; no external owning-maintainer sign-off is asserted. This successor preserves every legacy resource, maintenance, CLI and compatibility row below as defer / exclude. It adds no retirement authority and leaves v1 byte-identical. Historical source observations below remain tied to v1's `3d256e632a7645bc2261e668ac7c74be81155f58` pin, not the successor baseline. The new target table and this decision supersede the historical statements that no decorated Contracts can be enrolled.
+
